// yq-keepwarm: a Cloudflare Worker with Cron Triggers (Workers Free plan, 24-Sep-2026) that keeps the
// Render API warm and runs the shop's scheduled endpoints. It replaces the GitHub Actions cadence:
// keepalive.yml says "*/10" and shop-cron.yml "*/15", but GitHub throttles scheduled workflows on
// free public repos to a median gap of ~201 min (measured 21-24 Sep), so the API was cold (11-12 s)
// in business hours, assigned orders were never chased and the 08:00 agent hour was mostly missed.
// Both workflows stay as the backstop (keepalive.yml is also what keeps Supabase from its 7-day pause).
//
// Code: workers/keepwarm.js (no build step). Triggers, in UTC:
//   */10 3-19 * * *   GET /health                          06:00-22:59 Bahrain, every 10 min
//   */15 * * * *      GET the SCHEDULER_PATHS with X-Agent-Key (the same call shop-cron.yml makes)
// Both count as Worker requests: ~200/day against the free 100,000/day. Cron Triggers are free.
//
// DEPLOY (from web/, needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN + CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID in the env, like deploy_cf.py):
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 deploy -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 secret put AGENT_API_KEY -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc   (paste the Render value)
// The secret is the API's AGENT_API_KEY (the value behind the X-Agent-Key header); without it the
// scheduler leg logs an error and does nothing, the health leg still runs.
// Verify: Workers & Pages -> yq-keepwarm -> Triggers shows both crons; Logs (or
// `wrangler tail -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc`) shows "/health -> HTTP 200" lines. The Worker has
// no public URL (workers_dev off, no routes) - a dashboard "Send request" answers 404 by design.
{
  "name": "yq-keepwarm",
  "main": "workers/keepwarm.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-18",
  "workers_dev": false,
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  "vars": {
    "API_URL": "https://yq-ops-assistant.onrender.com",
    // Comma-separated; mirrors the loop in .github/workflows/shop-cron.yml. Trim to
    // "/scheduler/shop-jobs" if the agent reactions or the daily agents should stay on GitHub only.
    "SCHEDULER_PATHS": "/scheduler/shop-jobs,/scheduler/run-due,/events/dispatch"
  },
  "triggers": {
    "crons": ["*/10 3-19 * * *", "*/15 * * * *"]
  }
}
